# T2ROTF — repository ignore rules
#
# Nothing derived from the game and no build output is committed.
# The ~7 GB of game data (game/, update/, patched/, dlc/) and every build
# directory (recomp/out/, build/, out/, app/) stay out of the repository.

# --- Game data (never committed) ---------------------------------------------
game/
update/
patched/
DLC/
dlc/
assets/
$SystemUpdate/
extracted/
refs/
*.xex
*.xexp
*.iso
*.vpk

# --- Build output / intermediates --------------------------------------------
build/
out/
app/
recomp/out/
recomp/generated/default.bak_thunks/
recomp/generated/default_tu_bak/
_pkg_v*/
_tmp_pkg/
*.nro
*.nacp
*.elf
*.lst
*.map
*.o
*.obj
*.a
*.log
*.err
t2rotf_nm.txt
T2ROTF_switch_port.zip

# --- Reference clones (study material, not part of this project) -------------
repos/
reference_repos/
tools/xenia-canary/
tools/win/
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# --- Backups / scratch -------------------------------------------------------
*.bak
*.bak.*
icon_T2_bak.png
nul

# --- Environment / editor ----------------------------------------------------
.dumate/
.tmp/
.vs/
.vscode/

# --- Bundled ReXGlue SDK (sdk/) -----------------------------------------------
# sdk/ vendors the ReXGlue SDK (v0.10.0 + this port's Switch patches) so the
# repository is self-contained. Its sources, headers, templates, resources and
# third-party trees must all be tracked, even where the generic patterns above
# (*.a, *.o, *.obj, *.elf, *.lst, *.map, *.log, *.err, out/, build/) would
# otherwise match. Only SDK build output stays ignored.
!sdk/**
sdk/out/
sdk/build/
sdk/CMakeUserPresets.json